{
  "case_id": "2005-05-352",
  "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When did -- when did we first hold that the State had to provide counsel if -- if the defendant could not afford his own counsel?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0000-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I believe that Gideon was decided in 1963, Justice Scalia."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Johnson v. Zerbst, I believe, was in the '30s."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is that if there were a clear abuse of discretion, in accordance with the ordinary mandamus standards --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government's position is that he could seek a writ of mandamus, and if he qualified under the standards for mandamus, then he could obtain relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0000-0007",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the defendant, at the end of the day -- and if was the operative word -- could obtain automatic reversal, then the defendant's interests could be vindicated at the end of trial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Why -- why take it away from the 10 percent?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DREEBEN: I'm not suggesting that it be taken away. I think that it needs to be protected."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: It's a fair trial. Nobody is saying it wasn't a fair trial, but he didn't have the lawyer he wanted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could that not be harmless beyond a reasonable doubt?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Euel Lee case, which is a case where a black defendant wanted to go forward with his counsel of choice in -- in the District of Maryland, and he was forced to go ahead with a more experienced, establishment-type counsel and -- and to his detriment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, it's not contested in this case that the -- that the pro hac vice denial did violate the Sixth Amendment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you saying that this -- trial is -- is one thing. Appeal -- but you say he would do the appeal over? He'd do the appellate argument over?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are there cases in the records where it shows government overreaching or bad faith and so forth in trying to get rid of the counsel? That just doesn't happen?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What the United States is suggesting is that we should have these satellite collateral proceedings where we have to not just investigate questions like that perhaps, but also recreate an entire trial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would your rule apply in the case of a guilty plea?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, but then you wouldn't -- I'm sorry to interrupt you. But at that point, the defendant would be well advised to go ahead with trial with his second-choice lawyer. Right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: How many -- how many circuits are applying that rule?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondent's submission in the Eighth Circuit's holding in this case is fundamentally anomalous in two respects."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And it's anomalous factually because a defendant who is deprived of his first-choice counsel may have selected that counsel improvidently, may select his second-choice counsel with much greater care, may obtain a lawyer who is far more competent and far more effective, and all of those things have to be discarded on Respondent's view and the Eighth Circuit's holding and automatic reversal ordered, forcing society to bear the costs of a retrial even when there is no reasonable probability or it is a beyond a reasonable doubt that no lawyer could have made a difference."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-05-352",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "8133adc4926168871e9977892fc3cd584bac4a10af44cb6fd3692bf7cf1cadd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8133adc49261-0003-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "misunderstanding of this Court's Flanagan decision in which dictum was quoted as if it were a holding and because the courts failed to triangulate the right in question here with the right that this Court has recognized in the ineffectiveness context and in the conflicts context."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
